INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(395,'destination',73,'Liam Thomson',NULL,2.0,'Not sure if this is a scam or not. It feels like it''s been deserted and someone hasn''t been told it''s closed so still collecting the 20k per person.  Quite interesting to see the old village and how life used to be, but I''m not sure it has anyone looking after the grounds. It''s all very overgrown and run down. I wouldn''t make a trip to see it however if you are passing and would like to see the old houses on stilts then maybe 🤷','a month ago');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(396,'destination',73,'krisnarta sembiring',NULL,5.0,'The museum holds various collections from Bataknese culture. Sadly, the traditional houses are unoccupied and not maintained. I''m afraid they will be severely damaged soon. The glass house is the most attractive object according to me. It contains old furnitures from colonial era. The entrance ticket costs IDR 2000. The parking lot is sufficient. The museum is located beside the main road and is not difficult to find.','3 months ago');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(397,'destination',73,'Alice',NULL,5.0,'So we were brought here as part of a tour to see the Batak museum but you have to go just for the garden! The entrance fee is 20K per person which is barely anything for an incredibly view and beautiful flowers. The owner speaks good English and was very welcoming. She said she also runs a bed and breakfast (can be found on booking.com apparently).
