INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(479,'destination',89,'Fournis Gaëlle (Gayelle)',NULL,4.0,'Saya sangat suka tempat ini. Namun sayang tidak ada penjelasan dalam bahasa Inggris. Semuanya ditulis dalam bahasa Indonesia. 😕 Meski begitu, sambutannya sangat ramah, dalam bahasa Inggris yang baik, dan museum ini menawarkan beberapa karya yang sangat mengejutkan dan indah.','3 weeks ago');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(480,'destination',89,'Dennis',NULL,3.0,'Cool ancient pieces but very little information about the items and culture. We went through it in 10 minutes','3 weeks ago');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(481,'destination',89,'S Hardiyanti',NULL,3.0,'Museum ini terletak di antara pasar Tomok bagian ujung. Tidak ada lahan parkir di sekitar museum, parkir dapat didapatkan di sekitar rumah adat dan pertunjukan sigale-gale. Paket wisata budaya di satu wilayah Tomok antara lain pertunjukan sigale-gale, makan raja, dan museum batak. Dapat dilakukan dalam satu waktu. Petunjuk arah dan rute wisata ini kurang banyak, apalagi wisata berada di tengah pasar dan keramaian. Sehingga tidak dapat bnyak menikmati. Bangunan museum ini berbentuk rumah adat batak yang berisi koleksi barang-barang suku batak kuno. Namun hanya sedikit barang yang dilengkapi dengan penjelasan. Sehingga jika berkunjung tanpa tour guide sulit mendapatkan pemahaman yang lengkap.','2 months ago');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(482,'destination',89,'The Wandering Tofu',NULL,3.0,'Wandered into the Batak Museum in Tomok expecting the usual museum vibe… but nope, it was completely unmanned when we arrived—zero staff, zero lights. It felt like we had unlocked a bonus level of Night at the Museum: Batak Edition. Cue us creeping around with a mini torch, hunting for light switches like modern-day explorers. (found them, and yes, we felt like heroes.)
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(483,'destination',89,'The Compass Guy',NULL,4.0,'Batak Museum Tomok is where history stares at you with carved wooden eyes and centuries of side-eye. Housed in a small traditional Batak house that looks like it could either shelter ancestors or star in a gothic fairytale, this museum packs a lot of cultural soul into one sharp-roofed structure.
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(484,'destination',89,'Jeff Byron',NULL,5.0,'Great place to visit to get a bit of an understanding of batak culture. Spend the extra for a guide, it''s definitely worth it.','3 months ago');
INSERT INTO "reviews" VALUES(485,'destination',89,'Theodore H',NULL,5.0,'Worthwhile the visit. Lot of original Batak houses on display and you can even enter one of them.','4 months ago');
